userver provides installed CMake package targets. Core and chaotic are always
included; optional integrations are selected as vcpkg features.

  find_package(userver CONFIG REQUIRED COMPONENTS core postgresql chaotic)
  target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE userver::core userver::postgresql)

For unit tests and functional tests:

  find_package(userver CONFIG REQUIRED COMPONENTS core)
  target_link_libraries(service_unittest PRIVATE userver::utest)
  userver_testsuite_add_simple()

Example installation for a RealMedium-like service:

  vcpkg install userver[postgresql,utest,testsuite]

The grpc and scylla features are declared but intentionally fail with a clear
unresolved-dependency message until their missing pinned dependencies are
packaged. The old scylla-cpp-driver overlay is not used by userver[scylla].

The postgresql feature is currently limited to dynamic-linkage triplets because
the unpatched userver integration explicitly selects a shared libpq.
